---
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`Why ${SITE.name} exists, how the study workspace works, and credits for the pixel art.`}>
  <article class="prose prose-lg mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:font-semibold prose-a:text-plum sm:px-6">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <!-- Tip: this page matters to readers and to AdSense reviewers. Rewrite it in your own words and add your own story. -->
    <p>
      {SITE.name} started as a small collection of study videos that helped me through long revision days: pomodoro timers with pretty scenery, rain and library ambience,
      and short meditations for exam nerves. Over time it grew into what it is now: a free, cozy place to sit down and actually get the work done.
    </p>
    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={withBase('/workspace')}>The study workspace</a>: a pomodoro timer, task list and notepad, set in a pixel-art village that grows as you focus. Finished sessions earn coins for decorations, and new residents move in as your focus time adds up.</li>
      <li><a href={withBase('/videos')}>The video library</a>: a hand-picked set of study-with-me, ambience, focus-frequency and meditation videos.</li>
      <li><a href={withBase('/articles')}>Study guides</a>: practical write-ups on procrastination, planning, habits and deep focus, based on the books, talks and research that changed how I study.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Why a village?</h2>
    <p>
      Studying is mostly invisible progress. You can work hard for weeks before a grade or a skill shows it. The village makes the effort visible today: every session leaves
      something behind. It is a small reward tied to <em>showing up</em> rather than to results, which is exactly the habit worth building.
    </p>
    <h2>Your privacy</h2>
    <p>The workspace needs no account. Your tasks, notes and village are stored in your own browser. See the <a href={withBase('/privacy')}>privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
    <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
    <p>Learner's Landing mixes original art with free pixel-art packs from some very generous artists. Here's who made what.</p>
    <h3>Original to Learner's Landing</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bobby</strong> the alien and <strong>Psy-Koh</strong> the chameleon, the village's first two residents.</li>
      <li>All the shop decorations (trees, cottage, café, wizard tower and the rest) and the scenery behind the village.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Pixel-art packs</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://grafxkid.itch.io/sprite-pack-3" rel="noopener">Sprite Pack 3</a> by <strong>GrafxKid</strong> (CC0): residents J5 the robot, Gummy the gum bot, Twiggy,
        Tommy and Geralt.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://grafxkid.itch.io/sprite-pack-6" rel="noopener">Sprite Pack 6</a> by <strong>GrafxKid</strong> (CC0): residents Pip the penguin, Lumi the fairy, Sunny the
        orange and Sir Bones, plus the penguin on our 404 page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://notmatter.itch.io/2" rel="noopener">Little Animals Pack</a> by <strong>notmatter</strong>: residents Mochi the cat, Clover the bunny, Truffle the pig,
        Bramble the bear and Juniper the wolf.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://bdragon1727.itch.io/72-cute-pixel-character" rel="noopener">72 Cute Pixel Character</a> by <strong>bdragon1727</strong>: the characters you can pick
        as your own avatar.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Resident names are our own. Videos in the library belong to their creators and are embedded from YouTube.</p>
    <p>Got a suggestion or a video that helped you? <a href={withBase('/contact')}>Get in touch</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
